      "assessment": "R1 G4 correctly orients the overall Mean loss and observes Q4 gain with Q2/Q3 losses, but ignores the simultaneous early decrement when attributing the result to terminal escalation. Its H1 changes index2 yet cites index1 cosine/switching and claims twice the terminal displacement, whereas index2 has lower measured displacement. H1 [4,5,6,6] and H2 [5,5,5,6] are not selected.",
      "decision_update": "Require the full action diff and interval metadata before diagnosing a window. Preserve the Mean-versus-tail tradeoff without assigning each stratum to a time window absent joint evidence. Explicitly mark both future proposals unexecuted.",
