    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r01/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "424dc097a7620a13ab5dae8793867be5f8d1d867c65487bddc623f6514753c18",
      "assessment": "R1 synthesis chooses early extension, double-early extension, balanced increase and terminal restoration, correctly deduplicating [6,6,6,6]. It promotes the shared first tick of the higher-Mean schedules into the only plausible driver, although the arms differ in multiple coordinates and equal means could conceal offsetting effects. R2 Means are 4.060113, 4.075670, 4.126765 and 4.123541.",
      "decision_update": "Retain deduplication and a portfolio of interpretable component tests. Label shared-feature reasoning as a hypothesis, compare full paired distributions rather than equal aggregate means, and keep both Mean improvement and concentration visible.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Both early extensions underperform, while balanced guidance is best. This contradicts a monotone early-dose rule but does not prove late optimality; selected source groups are evidence, not the actual mixed restart parents.",
