      "assessment": "R2 G1 correctly diagnoses a loss after early extension and proposes restoring [6,5,5,4] or restoring plus terminal increase [6,5,5,5]. Only H1 is selected and reproduces Mean 4.123576 in R3. It again uses the 0-9 switching value for interval0 and treats the mixed incumbent as a uniform tick-5 population.",
      "decision_update": "Keep the evidence-driven reversal, but derive schedule and step identity from actual parent metadata. Distinguish repeatability under common RNG from independent evidence, and treat presumed matching-instability causality as unverified until candidate traces support it.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The restoration reproduces its historical Mean, while the failed extension was lower; this supports local directional sensitivity in the observed configuration, not a global optimum or a demonstrated matching-noise mechanism. H2 is not sampled in R3.",
